 is only a mechanism by which plugins can be reset. However, in this form it is confusing because it conflates with enabling or disabling plugins.\n\nI don't think this feature is a good idea. I'm not against reloading plugins (I even made a proposal for it: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13503) but by adding a menu item called 'Plugins' or whatever, we are creating two places where plugin operations can take place (project settings and in the menu), setting a precedent for moving more options there, and creating the expectation that the checkboxes are some sort of global state. ","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112086#pullrequestreview-4653969051","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112086","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112086#pullrequestreview-4653969051"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112086"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-08T12:14:53Z","commit_id":"cc37cb37f374cb5799fb609107e8aa72d8dfeb9f"}]